SailPoint Configuration
Authentication Flow: The SailPoint External Client App authenticates using the OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code Grant (Web Server Flow). 
 
 
Note:  SailPoint External Client App only supports OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code Grant Type.
The SailPoint team must complete the following configuration.
Step 1 - Enable ECA Toggle
Navigate to the Salesforce Source configuration in SailPoint.
Enable: Enable External Client App (ECA) toggle in SailPoint.
Step 2 - Enter Salesforce Details
Provide the following values:

Key	host_name
Value	https://login.salesforce.com (Production)
https://test.salesforce.com (Sandbox)

Step 3 - Add the parameter by clicking Add button
Step 4 - Click Authorize
User is redirected to the Salesforce login page.
Login using the User IdentityNow Service Account credentials.
•	Username
•	Password
Step 5 - Consent Screen
Review the requested permission and click: Allow
This grants SailPoint access to the Salesforce org.
After successful login, Salesforce displays the authorization screen.
Step 6 - Authentication Complete
After clicking Allow, Salesforce redirects back to SailPoint
Authentication completes and OAuth access/refresh tokens are issued.
The External Client App is now successfully authorized.

Validation
Validate the following after authentication:

•	Check the login the history of the Service account for any IP restrictions.
•	Authentication completes successfully.
•	SailPoint can connect to Salesforce.
•	Account aggregation works successfully.
•	Provisioning (if configured) functions correctly.
•	No authentication or permission errors are observed.
Troubleshooting Checklist
If authentication fails, verify:
•	External Client App package is installed.
•	ECA feature is enabled.
•	OAuth Setting is enabled in ECA.
•	Service Account is active.
•	Service Account has required permissions.
•	Login URL is correct.
•	Host Name is correct.
•	No Login IP restrictions block authentication.
•	SailPoint ECA toggle is enabled.
•	User clicked Allow on the Salesforce consent screen.

